{
  "id": "RLSA-2026:88477",
  "title": "Important: kernel security, bug fix, and enhancement update",
  "issued": {
    "date": "2026-10-24 12:08:27"
  },
  "updated": {
    "date": "2026-10-25 07:11:03"
  },
  "severity": "Important",
  "description": "The kernel packages contain the Linux kernel, the core of any Linux operating system.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* kernel: calipso: Don't call calipso functions for AF_INET sk. (CVE-2025-38147)\n\n* kernel: ipv4: raw: reject IP_HDRINCL packets with ihl \u003c 5 (CVE-2026-64114)\n\n* kernel: net/smc: reject CHID-0 ACCEPT that matches an empty ism_dev slot (CVE-2026-64048)\n\n* kernel: ALSA: hda/cs35l41: Fix firmware load work teardown (CVE-2026-64481)\n\n* kernel: fuse: re-lock request before returning from fuse_ref_folio() (CVE-2026-64266)\n\n* kernel: ipv4: fib: free fib_alias with kfree_rcu() on insert error path (CVE-2026-64572)\n\n* kernel: drm/amd/display: set new_stream to NULL after release (CVE-2026-68236)\n\n* kernel: ALSA: seq: close a re-opened queue timer in the destructor (CVE-2026-68202)\n\n* kernel: drm/dp/mst: fix buffer overflows in sideband chunk accumulation (CVE-2026-68278)\n\n* kernel: drm/amdgpu: fix lifetime issue of amdgpu_vm_get_task_info_pasid() (CVE-2026-68245)\n\n* kernel: ovl: check access to copy_file_range source with src mounter creds (CVE-2026-68448)\n\n* kernel: xfs: bounds-check buffer log item's dirty bitmap (CVE-2026-80536)\n\n* kernel: inet: frags: strip GSO state from fragments before reassembly (CVE-2026-80590)\n\n* kernel: drm/vmwgfx: use check_add_overflow for shader size+offset bound (CVE-2026-80887)\n\n* kernel: perf: Fix use-after-free when perf mmap() revival races with the last munmap() (CVE-2026-89791)\n\n* kernel: drm/amdkfd: Add TLB flush after MES queue eviction/suspension (CVE-2026-89811)\n\n* kernel: perf: Fix addr_filter_ranges lifetime (CVE-2026-93817)\n\n* kernel: drm/amdgpu: Bound GPIO I2C table entry count from VBIOS (CVE-2026-97493)\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* Backport request: bonding: only set speed/duplex to unknown, if getting speed failed [rhel-10.2.z] (JIRA:Rocky Linux-179066)\n\n* RTLA segfaults on freed memory access on double SIGINT [rhel-10.2.z] (JIRA:Rocky Linux-193031)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
